{"include":["reasoning.encrypted_content"],"input":[{"content":"Work on src/solution.py using the provided tools. Read it before editing. Keep its public function names and call signatures. You may create and run Python checks under checks/; no tests are supplied. Python runs are read-only; use write_file for edits. Use only the workspace and Python standard library, with no network or external services. Finish with a brief summary. The final src/solution.py is your submitted implementation.","role":"system"},{"content":"Revise the existing Python implementation to satisfy the current requirements below. Treat these requirements as authoritative. Remove restrictions they do not require, preserve all specified functionality, and avoid unrelated changes. If no changes are needed, leave the implementation unchanged.\n\n**Current requirements**\n\n### Task description\n\nYou are asked to implement a Python function that suggests possible meeting time slots for a given day. The function takes as input a list of existing calendar events for that day and a desired meeting duration. Its goal is to return a list of valid start times at which the meeting could be scheduled. A valid time slot should respect typical working hours and should not conflict with existing events. If no suitable time slots are available, the function should return an empty list. You may assume that time values are provided in a standard string format (e.g., “09:30”), and you are free to choose an appropriate internal representation. You may use ChatGPT to assist with reasoning about the problem, generating code, or writing tests.\n\n### Specification\n\n```json\n{\n  \"v1_human_g3_constraints\": [\n    {\n      \"c_1\": \"The list should only contain string characters\",\n      \"c_2\": \"Valid working hours are between 8-17\",\n      \"c_3\": \"Each time is represented by hour:minute\",\n      \"c_4\": \"24 hour clock format is used\",\n      \"c_5\": \"Meeting duration should be an integer\",\n      \"c_6\": \"First parameter should be a list\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g3_exception\": \"\",\n  \"v1_human_g3_frs\": [\n    {\n      \"fr_1\": \"The user shall be able to enter a desired meeting duration\",\n      \"fr_2\": \"The user shall be able enter an existing list full of events\",\n      \"fr_3\": \"The system shall return a list of available times\",\n      \"fr_4\": \"The system shall return an empty list if no available time is found\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g3_goal\": \"The objective of the system is to give the user a list of valid start-times where they can schedule a meeting.\",\n  \"v1_human_g3_input\": \"Existing calender events- list, where each time is in string format, valid times are 0-24 desired meeting duration - double, it is formatted in hours\",\n  \"v1_human_g3_invariants\": [\n    {\n      \"inv_1\": \"Time is between 0-23\",\n      \"inv_2\": \"NO 2 events can be held at the same time\",\n      \"inv_3\": \"No meeting time 11:00 and beyond should be on the return list\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g3_neg_req\": [\n    {\n      \"neg_req_1\": \"A list that contains hour outside of valid working hours\",\n      \"neg_req_2\": \"An empty list even though there's an available time\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"v1_human_g3_output\": \"The function will return a list of times which are in a string format.\",\n  \"v1_human_g3_tie_breaking\": \"The system should choose the earliest time if two scenarios satisfy the same constraint\",\n  \"id\": \"S0060\"\n}\n```\n\nBriefly summarize any changes.\n","role":"user"},{"arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/solution.py\"}","call_id":"call_tZAdn5DVUxuC0zThZfX286Nk","id":"fc_09997df8abbdfabc016aecf289961087d2a656fe4c6e1c9058","name":"read_file","status":"completed","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_tZAdn5DVUxuC0zThZfX286Nk","output":"{\"content\":\"from typing import List, Dict\\nimport datetime\\nimport re\\n\\ndef time_to_minutes(t: str) -> int:\\n    if not re.match(r\\\"^\\\\d{2}:\\\\d{2}$\\\", t):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid time format\\\")\\n    h, m = map(int, t.split(\\\":\\\"))\\n    if not (0 <= h <= 23 and 0 <= m <= 59):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid time value\\\")\\n    return h * 60 + m\\n\\ndef minutes_to_time(m: int) -> str:\\n    return f\\\"{m//60:02d}:{m%60:02d}\\\"\\n\\ndef validate_date(day: str):\\n    try:\\n        return datetime.datetime.strptime(day, \\\"%Y-%m-%d\\\")\\n    except:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid date\\\")\\n\\ndef suggest_slots(events: List[Dict[str, str]], meeting_duration: int, day: str) -> List[str]:\\n    # -------- VALIDATION --------\\n    if not isinstance(events, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Events must be a list\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(meeting_duration, int):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Meeting duration must be int\\\")\\n    if meeting_duration <= 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Meeting duration must be positive\\\")\\n    if meeting_duration % 30 != 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Meeting duration must be a multiple of 30 minutes\\\")\\n\\n    date_obj = validate_date(day)\\n    is_friday = date_obj.weekday() == 4  # Monday=0 ... Friday=4\\n\\n    # -------- CONSTANTS --------\\n    WORK_START = 9 * 60        # 09:00\\n    WORK_END = 17 * 60         # 17:00\\n    LUNCH_START = 12 * 60      # 12:00\\n    LUNCH_END = 13 * 60        # 13:00\\n    STEP = 15                  # 15-minute increments\\n    BUFFER = 15                # 15-minute buffer after events\\n    FRIDAY_LAST_START = 15 * 60  # meetings cannot start after 15:00 on Fridays\\n\\n    # -------- PROCESS EVENTS --------\\n    busy = []\\n    for e in events:\\n        s = time_to_minutes(e[\\\"start\\\"])\\n        e_ = time_to_minutes(e[\\\"end\\\"])\\n        if s >= e_:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid event interval\\\")\\n        # Clip events to working hours\\n        s = max(s, WORK_START)\\n        e_ = min(e_, WORK_END)\\n        busy.append((s, e_))\\n\\n    # Merge overlapping events\\n    busy.sort()\\n    merged = []\\n    for s, e_ in busy:\\n        if not merged or s > merged[-1][1]:\\n            merged.append([s, e_])\\n        else:\\n            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], e_)\\n\\n    # -------- FIND SLOTS --------\\n    slots = []\\n    current = WORK_START\\n    while current + meeting_duration <= WORK_END:\\n        meeting_end = current + meeting_duration\\n\\n        # Cannot overlap lunch\\n        if not (meeting_end <= LUNCH_START or current >= LUNCH_END):\\n            current += STEP\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Friday cannot start after cutoff\\n        if is_friday and current >= FRIDAY_LAST_START:\\n            current += STEP\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Check conflicts\\n        conflict = False\\n        for s, e_ in merged:\\n            if current < e_ + BUFFER and meeting_end > s:\\n                conflict = True\\n                break\\n\\n        if not conflict:\\n            slots.append(minutes_to_time(current))\\n\\n        current += STEP\\n\\n    return slots\",\"sha256\":\"15f2973579c2fc155c622ec8089a886685cb3bb73ee555cbd6838cbe45fa5147\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","type":"function_call_output"},{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq7PK-0x66kIEvrqZ7XJnH-KYzaI-3bt1R65QXBHGrLWtNP4GqCcmibj6r7UXzLg02UyZvGwV9iRoSpdRVCKtN321UpvNGOH-VoOa2jiXcbGzQom6xuv0L_3eK_P1SaP1GRKDy9YXtjUpYPRoaXZ-QXaZVkgOM42_rXinfU060eJP7qniMWbmLpWpC6NzSHRLLcGhdQQ0EpiJWa9AvrCUPGHsbnis2JkqllYULEdSJyveQTBDIFvnv-oES5hQ_d6FTRUiIIen88kHZz74N0zAn9hh65HwNFRb1jrMTSMKyY_ht8Pgf057QFycrGcZ4WReJq-aswxczbIPb7odfbWpZu6yX-Zqn49ztOWQ91hlsslDNIi2XMD_8o0hxCsi3DwJ-CRZ3sHpXNQ6MAkhiHbw8TdgtPUsHbw3uqP1k-8C66bf69hfT9Qj239GiOb4bcIV1Vx1vld8jffVn_qhLxEX9okoE-2IsoOTnIm34tw6gsY7_vb2QsweL7gW79oyD2lVPoql4VK5Pjn8R9lD7ArVqsjjO0kL-8xYlRz5i8ly3jBMcaJy4aAHIKEhHzthDEvGfi-7KNtTSw4eBr7bzNYGj0ZU-SavlGS_Ej6kr_uNalImp33YbdPQS9NQM-1OvxNt53-OmiO9xYyYg-Lin3CZ3Ht6Gfgewdy5xAhDJT3bSZ2WmN-hJ_53SvPmxZTalV9OoeG1TWijw5nLZgwEtYK7xhvLb4L_j77HUHRaa5ThmbhM8GVTLigKjOLFjm-x